  "body": "The source file is at 5.5MB, 121k lines.\r\n\r\nI wonder what's the overall opinion on splitting the source file into the same sections as the multipage output. \r\n\r\nIt could be as simple as letting ```html-build``` concatenate them and generate ```source``` again.\r\n\r\nEven if some sections are bigger than others, it feels this would make editing and reviewing changes a nicer process than currently is.\r\n\r\nThe biggest side effect would be that we would break the current open pull requests, but it's a one time pain.\r\n\r\nI could do the leg work of fixing `html-build` and doing the split, if it comes to that.\r\n\r\nI couldn't find a past issue pointing to this, so here it goes. What does everyone think about that?\r\n",
